{
  "name": "Speed-to-Lead — Radiant Aesthetics (demo)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Speed-to-Lead — Radiant Aesthetics (DEMO)\n\nDemonstration build. \"Radiant Aesthetics\" is fictional.\n\n**After import:**\n1. Re-map all credentials (GHL header auth, Slack, Google Sheets OAuth)\n2. Replace every `REPLACE_*` placeholder (GHL location ID, booking link, sheet ID, channel)\n3. Accept node typeVersion upgrades if your n8n build asks\n\n**Target:** first SMS out < 60 seconds from form submit.",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 400
      },
      "id": "sticky-overview",
      "name": "Sticky Note — Read Me First",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -740,
        260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 1 — Capture & normalize\n\nOne webhook receives leads from the website form and Meta lead-ad forwarders. The Code node flattens inconsistent payloads into one shape: split name, E.164 phone, lowercased email, source, service interest, timestamp.\n\nThis node absorbs most real-world breakage — new form fields land here, not downstream.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 460
      },
      "id": "sticky-stage1",
      "name": "Sticky Note — Capture",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -300,
        560
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 2 — Enrichment (placeholder, DISABLED)\n\nShips disabled on purpose — no fake vendor call. In a real engagement this slot becomes one of:\n- past-client lookup (GHL search by phone/email)\n- ad-campaign metadata join (UTM → campaign name)\n- a data-provider call if the client already pays for one\n\nDisabled nodes pass data through untouched, so the demo chain still runs end-to-end.",
        "height": 240,
        "width": 400
      },
      "id": "sticky-stage2",
      "name": "Sticky Note — Enrichment",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        140,
        560
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 3 — GHL upsert + instant outreach\n\n`POST /contacts/upsert` so repeat enquirers update, not duplicate. Then SMS + branded email via `POST /conversations/messages` — both land in the client's normal GHL inbox so the front desk can take over any thread.\n\nAuth: GHL **Private Integration token** as header auth (`Authorization: Bearer ...`) + `Version: 2021-07-28` header. SMS deliverability requires A2P 10DLC registration (US) — done inside GHL, not here.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 500
      },
      "id": "sticky-stage3",
      "name": "Sticky Note — GHL Outreach",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        580,
        560
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 4 — Notify + log\n\nSlack ping tells the owner the first touch already went out (no action needed yet). Google Sheets append is the plain-English audit trail the owner can open without logging into anything.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 420
      },
      "id": "sticky-stage4",
      "name": "Sticky Note — Notify & Log",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1120,
        560
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 5 — Wait 15 min → replied?\n\nPolls the GHL conversation for an inbound message.\n- Replied → humans own the thread from here.\n- No reply → escalate.\n\nThe reply-check condition reads `lastMessageDirection` on the most recent conversation — verify the response shape against the current LeadConnector API on go-live.",
        "height": 240,
        "width": 420
      },
      "id": "sticky-stage5",
      "name": "Sticky Note — Wait & Branch",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1580,
        560
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 6 — Voice AI callback (STUB — not built here)\n\nDeliberately a NoOp. GHL's Voice AI agent is configured **inside GHL** (AI Employee → Voice AI: script, guardrails, calendar access, transfer rules), not in n8n.\n\nIn production this handoff is either (a) an HTTP call that adds the contact to a GHL workflow which triggers the Voice AI callback, or (b) GHL's own no-reply automation owning this step entirely. Marked as a stub because pretending it's a built node would be theater.",
        "height": 280,
        "width": 460
      },
      "id": "sticky-stage6",
      "name": "Sticky Note — Voice AI Stub",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2100,
        640
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "radiant-new-lead",
        "responseMode": "onReceived",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "node-webhook",
      "name": "Lead Webhook (form / ad)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -260,
        400
      ],
      "webhookId": "radiant-new-lead-demo"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Normalize inconsistent form / ad payloads into one clean lead shape.\nconst raw = $json.body ?? $json;\nconst pick = (...keys) => {\n  for (const k of keys) {\n    if (raw[k] !== undefined && raw[k] !== null && String(raw[k]).trim() !== '') {\n      return String(raw[k]).trim();\n    }\n  }\n  return '';\n};\n\nlet firstName = pick('first_name', 'firstName');\nlet lastName = pick('last_name', 'lastName');\nconst fullName = pick('name', 'full_name', 'fullName');\nif (!firstName && fullName) {\n  const parts = fullName.split(/\\s+/);\n  firstName = parts.shift();\n  lastName = parts.join(' ');\n}\n\n// Phone → rough E.164. Demo assumes US 10-digit numbers; adjust to the client's market.\nlet phone = pick('phone', 'phone_number', 'phoneNumber', 'mobile').replace(/[^\\d+]/g, '');\nif (phone && !phone.startsWith('+')) {\n  if (phone.length === 10) phone = '+1' + phone;\n  else if (phone.length === 11 && phone.startsWith('1')) phone = '+' + phone;\n}\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    firstName: firstName || 'there',\n    lastName,\n    email: pick('email', 'email_address').toLowerCase(),\n    phone,\n    source: pick('source', 'utm_source', 'form_name') || 'website-form',\n    interest: pick('service', 'interest', 'treatment') || 'a treatment',\n    receivedAt: new Date().toISOString()\n  }\n}];"
      },
      "id": "node-normalize",
      "name": "Normalize Lead",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -40,
        400
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://example.com/REPLACE_ME_enrichment_endpoint",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "node-enrich",
      "name": "Enrichment (placeholder — disabled)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        180,
        400
      ],
      "disabled": true,
      "notesInFlow": true,
      "notes": "Placeholder. Wire a real lookup here (past-client match, campaign metadata, or a data provider). Disabled so the chain runs end-to-end without a fake call."
    },
